# Buttons must have a visible, solid background

A button that renders as bare text (no visible background) is a BUG, not a
style choice. This has shipped repeatedly. Follow these rules with zero
exceptions.

## Hard rules

1. Every `.app-btn` MUST also carry exactly one color variant class:
   `app-btn--primary`, `app-btn--secondary`, `app-btn--danger`,
   `app-btn--info`, or `app-btn--success` (defined unlayered in
   `src/index.css`). These set a SOLID `background-color` via Tailwind theme
   tokens (`var(--color-*)`), so the fill always renders.

   ```tsx
   // GOOD
   <button className="app-btn app-btn--secondary">Cancel</button>
   <button className="app-btn app-btn--primary w-full gap-2">Save</button>

   // BAD — no variant; relies on a Tailwind bg utility for the fill
   <button className="app-btn bg-slate-800/70 text-slate-200">Cancel</button>
   ```

2. NEVER use an opacity-modified background utility (`bg-<color>-<n>/<NN>`,
   e.g. `bg-slate-800/70`, `bg-purple-600/90`) as the *fill* of a button.
   - In Tailwind v4 these compile to `color-mix(in oklab, …)`, which renders
     invisibly / not at all on older Android WebViews — the button looks like
     plain text.
   - Tailwind background *utilities* are layered (`@layer utilities`) and can
     also lose the cascade to unlayered author rules + preflight.
   - Use a solid variant class instead. Opacity-modified colors are only for
     decorative/secondary layering (blurs, subtle card tints), never a button
     fill.

3. A button must never depend solely on `text-*` color to be visible. If you
   can read the label but see no button shape/fill, it is broken.

4. Add layout-only utilities (`w-full`, `gap-2`, `mb-3`, `ml-auto`,
   `touch-manipulation`, `shadow-sm`, …) alongside the variant freely. Disabled
   styling is handled by `.app-btn:disabled` — do not re-add
   `disabled:opacity-50`.

5. Ionic `IonButton` already provides a solid theme background and is exempt.

## Before finishing any UI change that adds/edits a button

- Confirm each `<button className="app-btn …">` includes an `app-btn--*`
  variant.
- Grep check: `app-btn[^"]*bg-` must return NO matches in `src/**/*.tsx`.

See `docs/coding-rules.md` and `tasks/lessons/button-backgrounds.md`.
